examples DelveTalk 1
case two artists approve the exact arrangement
law north south curator
as curator
send open
expect refusal: source refused: Opening requires both approvals of this exact arrangement.
as north
send offerNorth
  title: Fold
  note: A paper test piece.
  minutes (Nat): 4
  fragile (Bool): true
  light: dim
expect committed
as south
send offerSouth
  title: Thread
  note: A woven test piece.
  minutes (Nat): 6
  fragile (Bool): false
  light: bright
expect committed
as curator
send arrange
  caption: Fold meets Thread.
  first: south
expect committed
as south
send consentSouth
expect committed
as curator
send open
expect refusal: source refused: Opening requires both approvals of this exact arrangement.
as north
send consentNorth
expect committed
as curator
send arrange
  caption: An unapproved replacement.
  first: north
expect refusal: source refused: The curator must arrange both pieces once.
as curator
send open
expect result: Fold meets Thread.
as curator
send open
expect refusal: source refused: Opening requires both approvals of this exact arrangement.
observe north
  title: The Room Between
  prose: A paper test piece.
expect view
case artist identity and piece bounds belong to source
law north south curator
as south
send offerNorth
  title: Forged
  note: Another artist's piece.
  minutes (Nat): 4
  fragile (Bool): true
  light: dim
expect refusal: source refused: Only this artist may offer one valid piece before arrangement.
as north
send offerNorth
  title: Fold
  note: A paper test piece.
  minutes (Nat): 31
  fragile (Bool): true
  light: dim
expect refusal: source refused: Only this artist may offer one valid piece before arrangement.
as north
send consentNorth
expect refusal: source refused: Only this artist may approve the current arrangement once.
